  "nl_text": "The rschema_0338 database is used to store information about a college and its students, teachers, courses, and course enrollments. The database has five tables: College, Student, Teacher, Course, and Course_Enrollment_and_Grade.\nThe College table contains information about the college, including its location, name, total number of staff, and total number of students. The table has a primary key on the College_ID column.\nThe Student table contains information about the students, including their age, name, gender, registration time, and telephone number. The table has a primary key on the Student_ID column and a foreign key on the Associated_College_ID column that references the College table.\nThe Teacher table contains information about the teachers, including their age, name, gender, title, and contact information. The table has a primary key on the Teacher_ID column and a foreign key on the Associated_College_ID column that references the College table.\nThe Course table contains information about the courses, including the course name, classroom, class hours, and course summary. The table has a primary key on the Course_ID column and a foreign key on the Teaching_Teacher_ID column that references the Teacher table.\nThe Course_Enrollment_and_Grade table contains information about the course enrollments and grades, including the course ID, student ID, enrollment time, and course grade. The table has a primary key on the Student_ID, Course_ID, and Enrollment_Time columns.\nIn summary, the rschema_0338 database is used to store information about a college and its students, teachers, courses, and course enrollments. The database has five tables that are related to each other through foreign keys, and each table has a primary key that is used to identify the records.",
  "gold_question": "Academic administration system business requirement description: The school has multiple colleges, each with a college name, college location, total number of staff, and total number of students. Each college consists of multiple students and teachers. Each student has a Student ID, name, gender, date of birth, age, telephone, registration time, and associated college ID. Each teacher has a Teacher ID, gender, name, age, contact information, title, and associated college ID. The school offers multiple courses, each with a Course ID, name, credit number, teaching Teacher ID, course summary, class hours, and classroom. Students can enroll in multiple courses, and each enrollment requires recording the Student ID, Course ID, enrollment time, and course grade.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0338.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0338\nCREATE TABLE `College` (\n  `College_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Total_Staff` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Total_Students` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`College_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Student` (\n  `Student_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `Registration_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Telephone_Number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Associated_College_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Student_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Associated_College_ID`) REFERENCES `College` (`College_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Teacher` (\n  `Teacher_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Age` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `Title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Contact_Information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Associated_College_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Teacher_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teacher_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Associated_College_ID`) REFERENCES `College` (`College_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Course` (\n  `Course_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Course_Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Classroom` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Class_Hours` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `Course_Summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Teaching_Teacher_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Course_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Teaching_Teacher_ID`) REFERENCES `Teacher` (`Teacher_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Course_Enrollment_and_Grade` (\n  `Student_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Course_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Enrollment_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Course_Grade` varchar(2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Student_ID`, `Course_ID`, `Enrollment_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_enrollment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Student_ID`) REFERENCES `Student` (`Student_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `course_enrollment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Course_ID`) REFERENCES `Course` (`Course_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
